From: y52s recovery work
Subject: [PATCH] y52s: hand gatekeeper the raw digest, not its hex text

Run 42866203274 put the masked tag parser on the device and it worked: the
escrow key of app clone 999 now reports

  y52s: tied-profile key requires sid=0x779b8423e32ee87 type=3 auth_timeout=30s

so 0014 did its job -- the SID really is read out of the key now.  The next
step, minting a token for that SID from the synthetic password, fails:

  y52s: gk verify /data/system_de/0/spblob/0000000000000000.handle (uid 0):
        sid=0x779b8423e32ee87 call_ok=1 code=-1 timeout=0 token=0
  y52s: sid token: no enrolment accepted the synthetic password

call_ok=1 proves the HAL was reached; code=-1 (ERROR_INVALID) means the
secret did not match.  Both uid domains were tried (0 and 100000), so the
domain is not the problem -- the secret is.

The cause is a return-type mismatch.  AOSP's AuthenticationToken calls

  new SP800Derive(sp).withContext("sp-gk-authentication",
        "android-synthetic-password-personalization-context")

which returns a 32-byte byte[].  vold's helper with the same name and the
same HMAC construction returns the digest as a 64-character LOWERCASE HEX
STRING (see HashPassword.cpp: sprintf("%02x")).  The token code passed that
hex text to verify() as the password, so gatekeeper hashed 64 ASCII bytes
that never existed on the device -- hence -1 every time.

TWRP never noticed because its own FBE path uses the hex string directly as
the disk key (and that path works), so the helper looks correct in isolation.
The v2 branch had the identical bug: personalizedHash() also returns hex text
while AOSP returns the 64-byte SHA-512 digest.

Fix: decode the hex back to bytes before using it as the gatekeeper secret.
Nothing else changes -- same label, same context, same SP, no hardcoded value,
so this stays generic for every device that uses AOSP tied profiles.

Second, smaller fix in the same code path: when minting fails, /auth_token was
taken on faith.  On this device it held a stale token for sid=0xbbc2... which
begin() can only reject with -26.  It is now accepted only when it actually
carries the SID the key demands, and the log says why when it does not.

Expected trace once this is right:

  y52s: sid token: gk input 32 bytes (v3)
  y52s: gk verify ...(uid 0): sid=0x779b8423e32ee87 call_ok=1 code=0 timeout=0 token=115
  y52s: sid token: minted for sid=0x779b8423e32ee87 (user 0)
  y52s: tied-profile credential recovered (80 bytes)

---
--- a/Decrypt.cpp
+++ b/Decrypt.cpp
@@ -1108,6 +1108,37 @@
  *   v2: personalisedHash("sp-gk-authentication", sp)
  * Both label and context are AOSP constants.  The trap is the RETURN TYPE:
  * vold's helpers hand back hex text, AOSP hands back bytes -- see below. */
+/* vold's PersonalizedHashSP800()/PersonalizedHash() return the digest as a
+ * LOWERCASE HEX STRING, but gatekeeper wants the raw digest bytes: AOSP's
+ * SP800Derive.withContext() and personalizedHash() both return byte[].
+ * Handing the 64-character hex text to verify() makes every enrolment answer
+ * -1 (ERROR_INVALID) -- exactly what the device log showed:
+ *
+ *   y52s: gk verify ...(uid 0): sid=0x779b8423e32ee87 call_ok=1 code=-1 timeout=0 token=0
+ *
+ * so convert the hex back to bytes before using it as the gatekeeper secret.
+ * The digest length is whatever the helper produced: 32 bytes (SHA-256) for
+ * v3, 64 bytes (SHA-512) for v2 -- both are what AOSP hands to gatekeeper. */
+static bool Y52s_Hex_To_Bytes(const std::string& hex, std::string* out) {
+	out->clear();
+	if (hex.empty() || (hex.size() % 2) != 0)
+		return false;
+	for (size_t i = 0; i < hex.size(); i += 2) {
+		const char h = hex[i], l = hex[i + 1];
+		int hi, lo;
+		if (h >= '0' && h <= '9') hi = h - '0';
+		else if (h >= 'a' && h <= 'f') hi = h - 'a' + 10;
+		else if (h >= 'A' && h <= 'F') hi = h - 'A' + 10;
+		else return false;
+		if (l >= '0' && l <= '9') lo = l - '0';
+		else if (l >= 'a' && l <= 'f') lo = l - 'a' + 10;
+		else if (l >= 'A' && l <= 'F') lo = l - 'A' + 10;
+		else return false;
+		out->push_back((char)((hi << 4) | lo));
+	}
+	return !out->empty();
+}
+
 static bool Y52s_Mint_Sid_Token(const userid_t owner_id, uint64_t want_sid,
 		std::string* token_out) {
 	if (g_y52s_sp.empty() || g_y52s_sp_user != owner_id) {
@@ -1115,18 +1146,20 @@
 		       (int)owner_id);
 		return false;
 	}
-	std::string gk_input;
+	std::string gk_hex, gk_input;
 	if (g_y52s_sp_v3)
-		gk_input = PersonalizedHashSP800("sp-gk-authentication",
+		gk_hex = PersonalizedHashSP800("sp-gk-authentication",
 				PERSONALISATION_CONTEXT, g_y52s_sp.data(),
 				(int)g_y52s_sp.size());
 	else
-		gk_input = PersonalizedHash("sp-gk-authentication",
+		gk_hex = PersonalizedHash("sp-gk-authentication",
 				g_y52s_sp.data(), (int)g_y52s_sp.size());
-	if (gk_input.empty()) {
+	if (!Y52s_Hex_To_Bytes(gk_hex, &gk_input)) {
 		printf("y52s: sid token: gatekeeper input derivation failed\n");
 		return false;
 	}
+	printf("y52s: sid token: gk input %zu bytes (v%d)\n",
+	       gk_input.size(), g_y52s_sp_v3 ? 3 : 2);
 	std::vector<Y52sHandleCand> cands;
 	Y52s_Collect_Handles(&cands);
 	for (size_t i = 0; i < cands.size(); ++i) {
@@ -1445,10 +1478,25 @@
 		printf("y52s: key carries no USER_SECURE_ID, no token needed\n");
 	}
 	if (token_raw.empty() && want_sid != 0) {
-		printf("y52s: minting failed, falling back to /auth_token\n");
-		if (!android::base::ReadFileToString("/auth_token", &token_raw) ||
-		    token_raw.size() < 69)
-			token_raw.clear();
+		/* /auth_token is whatever the last gatekeeper verify left behind; it
+		 * is only usable if it actually carries the SID this key accepts.
+		 * On this device it held sid=0xbbc2... (a stale, unrelated token),
+		 * and feeding it to begin() can only return -26. */
+		std::string at;
+		if (android::base::ReadFileToString("/auth_token", &at) && at.size() >= 69) {
+			android::hardware::keymaster::V4_0::HardwareAuthToken probe = {};
+			if (Y52s_Parse_Token(at, &probe) && probe.userId == want_sid) {
+				token_raw = at;
+				printf("y52s: /auth_token carries the wanted sid=0x%llx\n",
+				       (unsigned long long)want_sid);
+			} else {
+				printf("y52s: /auth_token carries sid=0x%llx (type=%u), "
+				       "key wants 0x%llx - ignoring it\n",
+				       (unsigned long long)probe.userId,
+				       (unsigned)probe.authenticatorType,
+				       (unsigned long long)want_sid);
+			}
+		}
 	}
 
 	std::vector<uint8_t> nonce_vec(nonce.begin(), nonce.end());
